//@ mode: session
//@ expect: goal

// An `extern` signature disagreeing with the call: `pow` is declared binary,
// but the call passes one argument. The foreign-call elaboration demands the
// declared arity (proposal-ffi.md §2), so in total (REPL) lowering the mismatch
// is elided to a typed hole — reported as a goal rather than silently building
// a malformed call. This is the class of bug the FFI type mapping exists to
// catch before a single byte crosses the boundary.

extern "c" from "m" {
  def pow(base: f64, exp: f64) -> f64;
}

m.pow(2.0f64)
